  "system": {
    "description": "<p>You open a yawning chasm in the earth.</p><p>Draw a <strong>line</strong> up to <strong>10 spaces long</strong>, or a <strong>circle</strong> with a <strong>radius</strong> between <strong>1-2 spaces</strong>. Each space must be within <strong>30 spaces</strong> of you.</p><p>A fissure opens up in the selected area. It is <strong>2 spaces</strong> <strong>deep</strong> and lasts until the start of your next turn.</p><p>Each creature within the affected area must make an opposed <strong>Reflexes</strong> check or fall into the fissure. If it succeeds, it decides which side of the fissure to end up on.</p><p>A creature that falls into the fissure takes <strong>1 Damage</strong> from the fall and is <strong>Prone</strong>. As an <strong>Action</strong>, it can climb up the side with a <strong>6:1</strong> <strong>Body (Athletics)</strong> check.</p>",
